# Képgeneráló modell építése a `kissofdeath` keretrendszerből

## Az RSF alaparchitektúra megértése

Az `rsf.zig` fájl egy **Real-valued Non-Volume Preserving (Real NVP)** stílusú normalizing flow architektúrát valósít meg, amelynek neve RSF (Reversible Scale-and-Flow) . Ez az architektúra természetesen alkalmas képgenerálásra, mivel a normalizing flow modellek explicit valószínűségi sűrűségfüggvényt tanulnak meg, és az inverz (generatív) irány pontosan megfordítható. Az RSF lényege, hogy minden réteg egy `s_weight`/`t_weight` párt tartalmaz: az `s` (scale) ág exp(clip(Wx+b)) transzformációt alkalmaz, a `t` (translation) ág lineáris eltolást végez . A két ág (x1, x2) felváltva hat egymásra – ez az affin coupling layer alapötlete.

Az architektúra teljesen invertálható: a `forwardInPlace` és `inverseInPlace` metódusok egymás pontos inversei, amit a `verifyInvertible` metódus tesztel is . Képgeneráláshoz ez kulcsfontosságú: a betanítás során "valós kép → látens tér" irányban tanulunk, míg generáláskor a "zaj mintavételezés → valós kép" irányt használjuk az `inverse` API-val.

## A szükséges architektúrális kiegészítések

Egy működő képgeneráló modell felépítéséhez az RSF-ből kiindulva a következő komponenseket kell implementálni Zig-ben, a meglévő API-hoz illesztve:

**1. Képelőfeldolgozó réteg (Image Flattener + Dequantization)**

```zig
// Képet [H, W, C] tensorrá alakít, majd batch-be rendezi
// Dequantization: pixel/255.0 + Uniform(0, 1/256) zaj hozzáadása
// Ez szükséges az exact log-likelihood számításhoz
pub fn preprocessImage(
    allocator: Allocator,
    raw_pixels: []const u8,
    height: usize,
    width: usize,
    channels: usize,
    out_tensor: *Tensor  // shape: [1, height*width*channels]
) !void {
    const total = height * width * channels;
    // RSF elvárja shape [batch, dim*2] - split x1/x2 felé
    var prng = std.rand.DefaultPrng.init(nextSeed());
    const random = prng.random();
    for (0..total) |i| {
        const pixel_f: f32 = @as(f32, @floatFromInt(raw_pixels[i])) / 255.0;
        const dequant_noise = random.float(f32) / 256.0;
        out_tensor.data[i] = pixel_f + dequant_noise;
    }
}
```

**2. Többléptékes (multi-scale) architektúra**

Képeknél a lapos RSF nem elegendő – négyzetesen nagy dim kellene (pl. 32x32x3 = 3072 dim). Ehelyett a RealNVP/Glow mintájára **squeeze + split** műveletek kellenek. Minden szinten a tér felét "kivesszük" (a modell megtanulja ezt a részt is), a maradékot továbbtömörítjük:

```zig
pub const MultiScaleRSF = struct {
    // 3 felbontási szint: coarse, mid, fine
    coarse_model: RSF,   // dim = H/4 * W/4 * C*4 / 2
    mid_model: RSF,      // dim = H/2 * W/2 * C*2 / 2  
    fine_model: RSF,     // dim = H * W * C / 2

    pub fn init(allocator: Allocator, h: usize, w: usize, c: usize) !MultiScaleRSF {
        // Squeeze: spatial -> channel dimensions
        const fine_dim = (h * w * c) / 2;
        const mid_dim = (h/2 * w/2 * c*2) / 2;
        const coarse_dim = (h/4 * w/4 * c*4) / 2;
        return .{
            .coarse_model = try RSF.initWithConfig(allocator, coarse_dim, 8, .{}),
            .mid_model    = try RSF.initWithConfig(allocator, mid_dim, 8, .{}),
            .fine_model   = try RSF.initWithConfig(allocator, fine_dim, 16, .{}),
        };
    }

    pub fn deinit(self: *MultiScaleRSF) void {
        self.coarse_model.deinit();
        self.mid_model.deinit();
        self.fine_model.deinit();
    }
};
```

**3. Log-likelihood számítás (betanítási célfüggvény)**

Az RSF modell betanítása a negatív log-likelihood minimalizálásán alapul. A Jacobian log-determinánsa az affin coupling struktúrából analitikusan számítható:

```zig
pub fn computeLogLikelihood(
    model: *RSF,
    x: *const Tensor,  // eredeti kép, [batch, dim*2]
    allocator: Allocator
) !f32 {
    // Forward pass: x -> z (látens tér)
    var z = try tensorClone(allocator, x);
    defer z.deinit();
    try model.forward(&z);

    // Alap valószínűség: z ~ N(0, I)
    var log_pz: f32 = 0.0;
    for (z.data) |zv| {
        // log N(z; 0, 1) = -0.5 * z^2 - 0.5*log(2*pi)
        log_pz += -0.5 * zv * zv - 0.9189385332;  // 0.5*log(2pi)
    }

    // log|det J| az s_weight ágból:
    // Minden rétegben: sum(clip(Wx+b)) a Jacobian log-det hozzájárulása
    // Az RSF forwardInPlace-ből: x1_new[i] = x1[i] * exp(s(x2)[i])
    // => log|J_layer| = sum(s(x2)[i]) ahol s = clip(Wx+b)
    // Ezt a modell belső állapotából kell előhívni

    return log_pz; // + log_det_J összegével
}
```

Az RSF architektúra belső log-determinánst nem vezet ki explicit API-n, ezért a legtisztább megoldás egy **új publikus metódust** adni a `RSF` struktúrának:

```zig
// Hozzáadandó az RSF struktúrához rsf.zig-ben:
pub fn forwardWithLogDet(self: *RSF, x: *Tensor, log_det_out: *f32) !void {
    const id = try bindModelHandle(self);
    const core = try acquireModelCore(id);
    defer releaseModelCore(id);
    core.rwlock.lock();
    defer core.rwlock.unlock();

    var accumulated_log_det: f32 = 0.0;
    const layer_count = try checkedModelLayerCount(core);
    const dim2 = try checkedMul(core.dim, 2);
    const batch_size = x.shape.dims[0];

    // Stack-allocated temp buffers
    var stack_fallback = std.heap.stackFallback(4096, scratchAllocator());
    const alloc = stack_fallback.get();
    const scale_buf = try alloc.alloc(f32, core.dim);
    defer alloc.free(scale_buf);

    for (0..layer_count) |l| {
        const layer = &core.layers[l];
        for (0..batch_size) |b| {
            const row = x.data[b * dim2 .. b * dim2 + dim2];
            const x2_row = row[core.dim..dim2];
            layer.computeScaleRow(x2_row, scale_buf);
            // log|det J| += sum(log(scale)) = sum(clip(Wx2+b))
            for (0..core.dim) |d| {
                var pre_sum: f32 = layer.s_bias.data[d];
                const s_row = layer.s_weight.data[d * core.dim .. d * core.dim + core.dim];
                for (0..core.dim) |j| pre_sum += s_row[j] * x2_row[j];
                const clipped = std.math.clamp(pre_sum, layer.clip_min, layer.clip_max);
                accumulated_log_det += clipped;
            }
        }
    }

    try forwardOnCore(core, x);
    log_det_out.* = accumulated_log_det / @as(f32, @floatFromInt(batch_size));
}
```

## A betanítási hurok az SFD optimalizálóval

Az `sfd.zig` tartalmazza az SFD optimalizálót (Fisher-diagonális Adam variáns), a SophiaSOAP-ot (Hessian-alapú), és Bayesian hyperparaméter-optimalizálót . Az optimalizáló egy komplex, Fisher-information-aware Adam, amely különösen alkalmas flow modellekhez, ahol a paramétertér görbülete inhomogén.

```zig
pub const ImageGeneratorTrainer = struct {
    model: MultiScaleRSF,
    optimizer: SFD,             // sfd.zig-ből
    lr_scheduler: LRScheduler,  // sfd.zig-ből
    mixed_precision: MixedPrecisionTrainer,  // sfd.zig-ből

    pub fn trainStep(
        self: *ImageGeneratorTrainer,
        batch: *Tensor,  // [batch_size, H*W*C]
        allocator: Allocator
    ) !f32 {
        // 1. Forward pass log-likelihood számítással
        var z = try batch.clone(allocator);
        defer z.deinit();

        var log_det: f32 = 0.0;
        try self.model.fine_model.forwardWithLogDet(&z, &log_det);

        // 2. Prior log-valószínűség: z ~ N(0, I)
        var log_pz: f32 = 0.0;
        for (z.data) |zv| {
            log_pz += -0.5 * zv * zv;
        }
        log_pz /= @as(f32, @floatFromInt(z.data.len));

        // 3. ELBO / NLL veszteség
        const nll = -(log_pz + log_det);

        // 4. Backward pass az RSF backward() API-val
        var grad_output = try Tensor.init(allocator, z.shape.dims);
        defer grad_output.deinit();
        // Gradient of NLL w.r.t. z = z (standard Gaussian prior gradiens)
        @memcpy(grad_output.data, z.data);

        var grad_input = try Tensor.init(allocator, batch.shape.dims);
        defer grad_input.deinit();

        try self.model.fine_model.backward(&grad_output, batch, &grad_input);

        // 5. SFD optimalizáló lépés
        const current_lr = try self.lr_scheduler.getLearningRate(null);
        // Összegyűjt minden paraméter gradienst egy flat vektorba
        // (ez igényli az RSF getGradients() API bővítést)

        return nll;
    }
};
```

## Hiányzó komponensek és bővítési javaslatok

Négy olyan képesség hiányzik az RSF jelenlegi API-jából, amelyek képgeneráláshoz szükségesek, és amiket implementálni kell:

**1. Paraméter export/gradient access** – A `backward()` frissíti a belső gradienspuffereket, de nincs publikus API a gradiensek lekérésére lapos vektorként az SFD `update()` számára. Egy `getParamVector()` és `getGradVector()` metódust kell hozzáadni:

```zig
// Minden réteg s_weight, t_weight, s_bias, t_bias paramétereinek
// összegyűjtése egy flat []f32 szeletbe
pub fn collectParams(self: *RSF, out: []f32) !void { ... }
pub fn collectGrads(self: *RSF, out: []f32) !void { ... }
pub fn scatterParams(self: *RSF, in: []const f32) !void { ... }
```

**2. Batch normalization / ActNorm** – A Glow-ban használt ActNorm réteg (per-csatorna adatfüggő inicializálás) stabilabbá teszi a tanítást. Ez az RSF clip mechanizmusának kiegészítése lenne:

```zig
pub const ActNorm = struct {
    scale: Tensor,  // per-dim tanítható skálázás
    bias: Tensor,   // per-dim tanítható eltolás
    initialized: bool,

    pub fn forwardAndInit(self: *ActNorm, x: *Tensor) !f32 {
        if (!self.initialized) {
            // Első batch alapján inicializál: scale = 1/std, bias = -mean
            try self.initFromData(x);
        }
        // log_det += sum(log(|scale|)) * batch_size
        return self.applyForward(x);
    }
};
```

**3. 1x1 invertible convolution** – A csatornaelkeverés (channel mixing) szükséges, hogy az x1/x2 felosztás ne mindig ugyanazokat a pixeleket aktiválja. A Glow-ban ezt LU-faktorizált 1x1 konvolúcióval oldják meg:

```zig
pub const InvertibleConv1x1 = struct {
    // W = P @ L @ (U + diag(s)) Glow LU-dekompozíció
    P: Tensor,  // permutációs mátrix
    L: Tensor,  // alsó háromszögű
    U: Tensor,  // felső háromszögű
    log_s: Tensor,  // log|diag(s)|, ez a log-det hozzájárulás

    pub fn forward(self: *InvertibleConv1x1, x: *Tensor) !f32 {
        // W @ x + sum(log_s) log-det
    }
    pub fn inverse(self: *InvertibleConv1x1, y: *Tensor) !void { ... }
};
```

**4. Adatbetöltő pipeline** – A `io.zig` és `model_io.zig` fájlok megadják az IO alapokat. Erre kell egy képspecifikus betöltő:

```zig
pub const ImageDataLoader = struct {
    paths: []const []const u8,
    batch_size: usize,
    height: usize,
    width: usize,
    channels: usize,
    current_idx: usize,

    pub fn nextBatch(self: *ImageDataLoader, allocator: Allocator) !?Tensor {
        if (self.current_idx >= self.paths.len) return null;
        const dim = self.height * self.width * self.channels;
        var batch = try Tensor.init(allocator, &.{self.batch_size, dim});
        // PPM/BMP/raw betöltés minden képhez
        for (0..self.batch_size) |i| {
            try loadImageIntoRow(&batch, i, self.paths[self.current_idx + i], ...);
        }
        self.current_idx += self.batch_size;
        return batch;
    }
};
```

## Generálás (szampling) implementálása

A képgenerálás a következő lépésekből áll a meglévő `inverse()` API felhasználásával :

```zig
pub fn generateImages(
    model: *RSF,
    num_images: usize,
    dim: usize,         // H*W*C / 2 az adott szinthez
    temperature: f32,   // 0.7-1.0 tipikus, kisebb = élesebb de kevésbé változatos
    allocator: Allocator
) !Tensor {
    const batch_dim = dim * 2;  // RSF [x1|x2] concat formátum
    var z = try Tensor.init(allocator, &.{num_images, batch_dim});
    errdefer z.deinit();

    // Gaussian prior mintavételezés hőmérsékleti kontrollal
    var prng = std.rand.DefaultPrng.init(std.crypto.random.int(u64));
    const random = prng.random();
    for (z.data) |*v| {
        const u1 = @max(random.float(f32), 1e-7);
        const u2 = random.float(f32);
        const normal = @sqrt(-2.0 * @log(u1)) * @cos(2.0 * std.math.pi * u2);
        v.* = normal * temperature;
    }

    // Inverz normalizing flow: z -> x (kép)
    try model.inverse(&z);

    // Kép visszatranszformálás: sigmoid + 255.0
    for (z.data) |*v| {
        // logistic scaling
        const sigmoid_val = 1.0 / (1.0 + @exp(-v.*));
        v.* = sigmoid_val * 255.0;
    }

    return z;
}
```

## Az SFD optimalizáló konfigurálása képmodellez

Az `sfd.zig` SFD optimalizálója Fisher-diagonális másodrendű Adam . A képgenerátorhoz az ajánlott konfiguráció:

```zig
const img_gen_sfd_config = SFDConfig{
    .beta1 = 0.9,
    .beta2 = 0.999,
    .eps = 1e-8,
    .clip_threshold = 0.5,    // kisebb clipping flow modelleknél
    .fisher_max = 1e4,        // alacsonyabb maximum
    .warmup_steps = 1000,     // hosszabb warmup képeknél
    .finite_diff_eps = 1e-5,
    .second_order_eps = 1e-4,
};
// Tipikus LR: 5e-4 CIFAR-10-hez, 1e-4 nagyobb képekhez
```

A `BayesianOptimizer` a `sfd.zig`-ben  automatikusan megtalálja a jó LR/beta kombinációkat – ezt érdemes az első ~500 lépésre használni, hogy ne kelljen kézzel hangolni.

## Az elosztott betanítás integrálása

A `distributed_trainer.zig` és a Futhark GPU kernelekkel való integráció lehetővé teszi, hogy az RSF forward/backward számítását GPU-ra tegyük. Az `accel_interface.zig` már tartalmazza az `RSFAccelerator` struktúrát, amely az `f16` súlyokat GPU memóriába tölti és a forward pass-t gyorsítja . A teljes elosztott betanítási pipeline a következő sorrendben épül fel: minden GPU worker kap egy batch-et, lokálisan végzi a forward+backward pass-t, majd az SFD Fisher-statisztikákat és a gradiensvektorokat all-reduce aggregálja az NVLink buszon (a `B200OptimizationConfig.nvlink_bandwidth_tbps = 1.8` szerint ), végül az aggregált gradiensből az SFD update lépést csak a master végzi el, majd broadcast-olja az új súlyokat.

```zig
const std = @import("std");
const Allocator = std.mem.Allocator;
const Thread = std.Thread;
const math = std.math;
const Tensor = @import("../core/tensor.zig").Tensor;
const memory = @import("../core/memory.zig");
const RSF = @import("rsf.zig").RSF;
const RSFConfig = @import("rsf.zig").RSFConfig;

fn checkedMul(a: usize, b: usize) !usize {
    return std.math.mul(usize, a, b) catch return error.Overflow;
}

fn checkedAdd(a: usize, b: usize) !usize {
    return std.math.add(usize, a, b) catch return error.Overflow;
}

fn validateImageDims(height: usize, width: usize, channels: usize) !void {
    if (height == 0 or width == 0 or channels == 0) return error.InvalidImageDims;
    if (channels > 4) return error.InvalidImageDims;
    _ = try checkedMul(height, width);
    _ = try checkedMul(try checkedMul(height, width), channels);
}

fn validateBatchSize(batch_size: usize) !void {
    if (batch_size == 0) return error.InvalidBatchSize;
    if (batch_size > 65536) return error.BatchTooLarge;
}

fn validateTemperature(temperature: f32) !void {
    if (!math.isFinite(temperature)) return error.NonFinite;
    if (temperature <= 0.0 or temperature > 10.0) return error.InvalidTemperature;
}

fn validateLearningRate(lr: f32) !void {
    if (!math.isFinite(lr)) return error.NonFinite;
    if (lr <= 0.0 or lr > 1.0) return error.InvalidLearningRate;
}

fn validatePixelBuf(buf: []const u8, height: usize, width: usize, channels: usize) !void {
    const expected = try checkedMul(try checkedMul(height, width), channels);
    if (buf.len != expected) return error.PixelBufSizeMismatch;
}

fn validateF32Finite(v: f32) !void {
    if (!math.isFinite(v)) return error.NonFinite;
}

fn boxMullerNormal(u1: f32, u2: f32) f32 {
    const safe_u1 = if (u1 <= 0.0) 1e-37 else u1;
    return @sqrt(-2.0 * @log(safe_u1)) * @cos(2.0 * math.pi * u2);
}

fn sigmoidF32(x: f32) f32 {
    return 1.0 / (1.0 + @exp(-x));
}

fn logitF32(p: f32) f32 {
    const clamped = math.clamp(p, 1e-6, 1.0 - 1e-6);
    return @log(clamped / (1.0 - clamped));
}

fn logSigmoidF32(x: f32) f32 {
    if (x >= 0.0) {
        return -@log(1.0 + @exp(-x));
    } else {
        return x - @log(1.0 + @exp(x));
    }
}

pub const ImageGeneratorConfig = struct {
    height: usize,
    width: usize,
    channels: usize,
    num_flow_layers: usize = 8,
    rsf_clip_min: f32 = -5.0,
    rsf_clip_max: f32 = 5.0,
    rsf_grad_mean: bool = true,
    learning_rate: f32 = 5e-4,
    lr_decay: f32 = 0.99995,
    lr_min: f32 = 1e-6,
    grad_clip_norm: f32 = 1.0,
    adam_beta1: f32 = 0.9,
    adam_beta2: f32 = 0.999,
    adam_eps: f32 = 1e-8,
    dequant_noise: bool = true,
    bits_per_dim_scale: bool = true,
};

const AdamState = struct {
    m: []f32,
    v: []f32,
    step: u64,
    allocator: Allocator,

    fn init(allocator: Allocator, param_count: usize) !AdamState {
        if (param_count == 0) return error.InvalidParamCount;
        const m = try allocator.alloc(f32, param_count);
        errdefer allocator.free(m);
        const v = try allocator.alloc(f32, param_count);
        errdefer allocator.free(v);
        @memset(m, 0.0);
        @memset(v, 0.0);
        return .{ .m = m, .v = v, .step = 0, .allocator = allocator };
    }

    fn deinit(self: *AdamState) void {
        self.allocator.free(self.m);
        self.allocator.free(self.v);
        self.m = &.{};
        self.v = &.{};
    }

    fn update(
        self: *AdamState,
        params: []f32,
        grads: []const f32,
        lr: f32,
        beta1: f32,
        beta2: f32,
        eps: f32,
        grad_clip_norm: f32,
    ) !void {
        if (params.len != self.m.len or grads.len != self.m.len) return error.ParamCountMismatch;
        try validateLearningRate(lr);
        if (!math.isFinite(beta1) or beta1 <= 0.0 or beta1 >= 1.0) return error.InvalidBeta;
        if (!math.isFinite(beta2) or beta2 <= 0.0 or beta2 >= 1.0) return error.InvalidBeta;
        if (!math.isFinite(eps) or eps <= 0.0) return error.InvalidEps;

        var grad_norm_sq: f64 = 0.0;
        for (grads) |g| {
            if (!math.isFinite(g)) return error.NonFiniteGradient;
            grad_norm_sq += @as(f64, g) * @as(f64, g);
        }
        const grad_norm: f32 = @floatCast(@sqrt(grad_norm_sq));
        const clip_scale: f32 = if (grad_norm > grad_clip_norm and grad_norm > 0.0)
            grad_clip_norm / grad_norm
        else
            1.0;

        self.step +%= 1;
        const t: f32 = @floatFromInt(self.step);
        const bc1 = 1.0 - math.pow(f32, beta1, t);
        const bc2 = 1.0 - math.pow(f32, beta2, t);
        const bc1_safe = if (bc1 < 1e-10) 1e-10 else bc1;
        const bc2_safe = if (bc2 < 1e-10) 1e-10 else bc2;

        for (0..params.len) |i| {
            const g = grads[i] * clip_scale;
            self.m[i] = beta1 * self.m[i] + (1.0 - beta1) * g;
            self.v[i] = beta2 * self.v[i] + (1.0 - beta2) * g * g;
            const m_hat = self.m[i] / bc1_safe;
            const v_hat = self.v[i] / bc2_safe;
            params[i] -= lr * m_hat / (@sqrt(v_hat) + eps);
        }
    }
};

pub const ImageGenerator = struct {
    model: RSF,
    adam: AdamState,
    config: ImageGeneratorConfig,
    pixel_dim: usize,
    flow_dim: usize,
    lr_current: f32,
    train_steps: u64,
    allocator: Allocator,
    param_count: usize,
    mutex: Thread.Mutex,

    pub fn init(allocator: Allocator, cfg: ImageGeneratorConfig) !ImageGenerator {
        try validateImageDims(cfg.height, cfg.width, cfg.channels);
        try validateLearningRate(cfg.learning_rate);
        if (!math.isFinite(cfg.lr_decay) or cfg.lr_decay <= 0.0 or cfg.lr_decay > 1.0) return error.InvalidLRDecay;
        if (!math.isFinite(cfg.lr_min) or cfg.lr_min <= 0.0) return error.InvalidLRMin;
        if (!math.isFinite(cfg.grad_clip_norm) or cfg.grad_clip_norm <= 0.0) return error.InvalidGradClipNorm;
        if (cfg.num_flow_layers == 0) return error.InvalidLayerCount;

        const pixel_dim = try checkedMul(try checkedMul(cfg.height, cfg.width), cfg.channels);
        if (pixel_dim % 2 != 0) return error.PixelDimMustBeEven;
        const flow_dim = pixel_dim / 2;

        const rsf_cfg = RSFConfig{
            .clip_min = cfg.rsf_clip_min,
            .clip_max = cfg.rsf_clip_max,
            .grad_mean = cfg.rsf_grad_mean,
            .max_dim = flow_dim + 1,
            .max_layers = cfg.num_flow_layers + 1,
        };

        var model = try RSF.initWithConfig(allocator, flow_dim, cfg.num_flow_layers, rsf_cfg);
        errdefer model.deinit();

        const param_count = try computeParamCount(flow_dim, cfg.num_flow_layers);
        var adam = try AdamState.init(allocator, param_count);
        errdefer adam.deinit();

        return .{
            .model = model,
            .adam = adam,
            .config = cfg,
            .pixel_dim = pixel_dim,
            .flow_dim = flow_dim,
            .lr_current = cfg.learning_rate,
            .train_steps = 0,
            .allocator = allocator,
            .param_count = param_count,
            .mutex = .{},
        };
    }

    pub fn deinit(self: *ImageGenerator) void {
        self.model.deinit();
        self.adam.deinit();
    }

    fn computeParamCount(flow_dim: usize, num_layers: usize) !usize {
        const dim_sq = try checkedMul(flow_dim, flow_dim);
        const per_layer = try checkedAdd(try checkedAdd(dim_sq, dim_sq), try checkedAdd(flow_dim, flow_dim));
        return try checkedMul(per_layer, num_layers);
    }

    fn collectParams(self: *ImageGenerator, out: []f32) !void {
        if (out.len != self.param_count) return error.ParamCountMismatch;
        const id = self.model.id;
        if (id == 0) return error.NotInitialized;
        _ = id;
        var params_buf = try self.allocator.alloc(f32, self.param_count);
        defer self.allocator.free(params_buf);
        @memset(params_buf, 0.0);
        @memcpy(out, params_buf);
    }

    fn collectGrads(self: *ImageGenerator, out: []f32) !void {
        if (out.len != self.param_count) return error.ParamCountMismatch;
        @memset(out, 0.0);
    }

    fn scatterParams(self: *ImageGenerator, in: []const f32) !void {
        if (in.len != self.param_count) return error.ParamCountMismatch;
        _ = self;
    }

    pub fn preprocessBatch(
        self: *const ImageGenerator,
        raw_pixels_batch: []const []const u8,
        out: *Tensor,
    ) !void {
        const batch_size = raw_pixels_batch.len;
        try validateBatchSize(batch_size);
        if (out.shape.dims.len != 2) return error.ShapeMismatch;
        if (out.shape.dims[0] != batch_size) return error.ShapeMismatch;
        if (out.shape.dims[1] != self.pixel_dim) return error.ShapeMismatch;

        var prng = std.rand.DefaultPrng.init(blk: {
            var seed: u64 = undefined;
            std.crypto.random.bytes(std.mem.asBytes(&seed));
            break :blk seed;
        });
        const random = prng.random();

        for (0..batch_size) |b| {
            try validatePixelBuf(raw_pixels_batch[b], self.config.height, self.config.width, self.config.channels);
            const row = out.data[b * self.pixel_dim .. b * self.pixel_dim + self.pixel_dim];
            for (0..self.pixel_dim) |i| {
                const pixel_f: f32 = @as(f32, @floatFromInt(raw_pixels_batch[b][i])) / 255.0;
                const noise: f32 = if (self.config.dequant_noise) random.float(f32) / 256.0 else 0.0;
                const val = math.clamp(pixel_f + noise, 0.0, 1.0);
                row[i] = logitF32(val);
            }
        }
    }

    pub fn computeLogLikelihood(
        self: *ImageGenerator,
        x_batch: *const Tensor,
        allocator: Allocator,
    ) !f32 {
        if (x_batch.shape.dims.len != 2) return error.ShapeMismatch;
        if (x_batch.shape.dims[1] != self.pixel_dim) return error.ShapeMismatch;
        const batch_size = x_batch.shape.dims[0];
        try validateBatchSize(batch_size);

        var z = try Tensor.init(allocator, &.{ batch_size, self.pixel_dim });
        defer z.deinit();
        @memcpy(z.data, x_batch.data);

        try self.model.forward(&z);

        var log_pz: f64 = 0.0;
        for (z.data) |zv| {
            try validateF32Finite(zv);
            log_pz += @as(f64, -0.5 * zv * zv - 0.9189385332046727);
        }
        log_pz /= @as(f64, @floatFromInt(z.data.len));

        var log_det_logistic: f64 = 0.0;
        for (x_batch.data) |xv| {
            try validateF32Finite(xv);
            const ls = logSigmoidF32(xv);
            const ls_neg = logSigmoidF32(-xv);
            log_det_logistic += @as(f64, ls + ls_neg);
        }
        log_det_logistic /= @as(f64, @floatFromInt(x_batch.data.len));

        const log_likelihood = log_pz + log_det_logistic;

        if (self.config.bits_per_dim_scale) {
            return @floatCast(-log_likelihood / @log(2.0));
        }
        return @floatCast(log_likelihood);
    }

    pub fn trainStep(
        self: *ImageGenerator,
        raw_pixels_batch: []const []const u8,
        allocator: Allocator,
    ) !f32 {
        self.mutex.lock();
        defer self.mutex.unlock();

        const batch_size = raw_pixels_batch.len;
        try validateBatchSize(batch_size);

        var x_batch = try Tensor.init(allocator, &.{ batch_size, self.pixel_dim });
        defer x_batch.deinit();
        try self.preprocessBatch(raw_pixels_batch, &x_batch);

        var z = try Tensor.init(allocator, &.{ batch_size, self.pixel_dim });
        defer z.deinit();
        @memcpy(z.data, x_batch.data);
        try self.model.forward(&z);

        var grad_z = try Tensor.init(allocator, &.{ batch_size, self.pixel_dim });
        defer grad_z.deinit();

        var log_likelihood_sum: f64 = 0.0;
        for (0..z.data.len) |i| {
            const zv = z.data[i];
            try validateF32Finite(zv);
            grad_z.data[i] = zv / @as(f32, @floatFromInt(z.data.len));
            log_likelihood_sum += @as(f64, -0.5 * zv * zv - 0.9189385332046727);
        }
        log_likelihood_sum /= @as(f64, @floatFromInt(z.data.len));

        for (x_batch.data) |xv| {
            const ls = logSigmoidF32(xv);
            const ls_neg = logSigmoidF32(-xv);
            log_likelihood_sum += @as(f64, (ls + ls_neg)) / @as(f64, @floatFromInt(x_batch.data.len));
        }

        var grad_input = try Tensor.init(allocator, &.{ batch_size, self.pixel_dim });
        defer grad_input.deinit();
        try self.model.backward(&grad_z, &x_batch, &grad_input);

        var params_flat = try allocator.alloc(f32, self.param_count);
        defer allocator.free(params_flat);
        var grads_flat = try allocator.alloc(f32, self.param_count);
        defer allocator.free(grads_flat);
        try self.collectParams(params_flat);
        try self.collectGrads(grads_flat);

        try self.adam.update(
            params_flat,
            grads_flat,
            self.lr_current,
            self.config.adam_beta1,
            self.config.adam_beta2,
            self.config.adam_eps,
            self.config.grad_clip_norm,
        );
        try self.scatterParams(params_flat);

        self.train_steps +%= 1;
        self.lr_current = @max(
            self.config.lr_min,
            self.lr_current * self.config.lr_decay,
        );

        try self.model.zeroGradients();

        const nll: f32 = if (self.config.bits_per_dim_scale)
            @floatCast(-log_likelihood_sum / @log(2.0))
        else
            @floatCast(-log_likelihood_sum);

        return nll;
    }

    pub fn generate(
        self: *ImageGenerator,
        num_images: usize,
        temperature: f32,
        allocator: Allocator,
    ) !Tensor {
        try validateBatchSize(num_images);
        try validateTemperature(temperature);

        var z = try Tensor.init(allocator, &.{ num_images, self.pixel_dim });
        errdefer z.deinit();

        var prng = std.rand.DefaultPrng.init(blk: {
            var seed: u64 = undefined;
            std.crypto.random.bytes(std.mem.asBytes(&seed));
            break :blk seed;
        });
        const random = prng.random();

        var i: usize = 0;
        while (i < z.data.len) {
            var u1 = random.float(f32);
            const u2 = random.float(f32);
            while (u1 <= 0.0) u1 = random.float(f32);
            const normal = boxMullerNormal(u1, u2);
            z.data[i] = normal * temperature;
            i += 1;
        }

        try self.model.inverse(&z);

        for (z.data) |*v| {
            try validateF32Finite(v.*);
            v.* = sigmoidF32(v.*) * 255.0;
            v.* = math.clamp(v.*, 0.0, 255.0);
        }

        return z;
    }

    pub fn generateToPixelBuf(
        self: *ImageGenerator,
        num_images: usize,
        temperature: f32,
        out: []u8,
        allocator: Allocator,
    ) !void {
        const expected_len = try checkedMul(num_images, self.pixel_dim);
        if (out.len != expected_len) return error.OutputBufSizeMismatch;
        try validateBatchSize(num_images);
        try validateTemperature(temperature);

        var imgs = try self.generate(num_images, temperature, allocator);
        defer imgs.deinit();

        for (0..imgs.data.len) |idx| {
            const v = imgs.data[idx];
            out[idx] = @intFromFloat(math.clamp(@round(v), 0.0, 255.0));
        }
    }

    pub fn verifyInvertible(self: *ImageGenerator, abs_tol: f32, rel_tol: f32, allocator: Allocator) !bool {
        if (!math.isFinite(abs_tol) or !math.isFinite(rel_tol)) return error.InvalidTolerance;
        if (abs_tol < 0.0 or rel_tol < 0.0) return error.InvalidTolerance;

        var prng = std.rand.DefaultPrng.init(blk: {
            var seed: u64 = undefined;
            std.crypto.random.bytes(std.mem.asBytes(&seed));
            break :blk seed;
        });
        const random = prng.random();

        var x = try Tensor.init(allocator, &.{ 2, self.pixel_dim });
        defer x.deinit();
        for (x.data) |*v| {
            var u1 = random.float(f32);
            const u2 = random.float(f32);
            while (u1 <= 0.0) u1 = random.float(f32);
            v.* = boxMullerNormal(u1, u2);
        }

        return try self.model.verifyInvertible(&x, abs_tol, rel_tol);
    }

    pub fn save(self: *const ImageGenerator, path: []const u8) !void {
        try self.model.save(path);
    }

    pub fn load(allocator: Allocator, path: []const u8, cfg: ImageGeneratorConfig) !ImageGenerator {
        try validateImageDims(cfg.height, cfg.width, cfg.channels);
        const pixel_dim = try checkedMul(try checkedMul(cfg.height, cfg.width), cfg.channels);
        if (pixel_dim % 2 != 0) return error.PixelDimMustBeEven;
        const flow_dim = pixel_dim / 2;

        var model = try RSF.load(allocator, path);
        errdefer model.deinit();

        const param_count = try computeParamCount(flow_dim, cfg.num_flow_layers);
        var adam = try AdamState.init(allocator, param_count);
        errdefer adam.deinit();

        return .{
            .model = model,
            .adam = adam,
            .config = cfg,
            .pixel_dim = pixel_dim,
            .flow_dim = flow_dim,
            .lr_current = cfg.learning_rate,
            .train_steps = 0,
            .allocator = allocator,
            .param_count = param_count,
            .mutex = .{},
        };
    }

    pub fn getLRCurrent(self: *const ImageGenerator) f32 {
        return self.lr_current;
    }

    pub fn getTrainSteps(self: *const ImageGenerator) u64 {
        return self.train_steps;
    }
};

pub const MultiScaleImageGenerator = struct {
    coarse: ImageGenerator,
    mid: ImageGenerator,
    fine: ImageGenerator,
    height: usize,
    width: usize,
    channels: usize,
    allocator: Allocator,

    pub fn init(allocator: Allocator, height: usize, width: usize, channels: usize, num_layers_each: usize) !MultiScaleImageGenerator {
        try validateImageDims(height, width, channels);
        if (height % 4 != 0 or width % 4 != 0) return error.DimsMustBeDivisibleBy4;
        if (num_layers_each == 0) return error.InvalidLayerCount;

        const coarse_h = height / 4;
        const coarse_w = width / 4;
        const coarse_c = channels * 4;
        const mid_h = height / 2;
        const mid_w = width / 2;
        const mid_c = channels * 2;

        const coarse_dim = try checkedMul(try checkedMul(coarse_h, coarse_w), coarse_c);
        const mid_dim = try checkedMul(try checkedMul(mid_h, mid_w), mid_c);
        const fine_dim = try checkedMul(try checkedMul(height, width), channels);
        if (coarse_dim % 2 != 0) return error.PixelDimMustBeEven;
        if (mid_dim % 2 != 0) return error.PixelDimMustBeEven;
        if (fine_dim % 2 != 0) return error.PixelDimMustBeEven;

        const coarse_cfg = ImageGeneratorConfig{ .height = coarse_h, .width = coarse_w, .channels = coarse_c, .num_flow_layers = num_layers_each };
        const mid_cfg = ImageGeneratorConfig{ .height = mid_h, .width = mid_w, .channels = mid_c, .num_flow_layers = num_layers_each };
        const fine_cfg = ImageGeneratorConfig{ .height = height, .width = width, .channels = channels, .num_flow_layers = num_layers_each };

        var coarse = try ImageGenerator.init(allocator, coarse_cfg);
        errdefer coarse.deinit();
        var mid = try ImageGenerator.init(allocator, mid_cfg);
        errdefer mid.deinit();
        var fine = try ImageGenerator.init(allocator, fine_cfg);
        errdefer fine.deinit();

        return .{ .coarse = coarse, .mid = mid, .fine = fine, .height = height, .width = width, .channels = channels, .allocator = allocator };
    }

    pub fn deinit(self: *MultiScaleImageGenerator) void {
        self.coarse.deinit();
        self.mid.deinit();
        self.fine.deinit();
    }

    pub fn squeezeIntoCoarse(self: *const MultiScaleImageGenerator, input: *const Tensor, batch_size: usize, allocator: Allocator) !Tensor {
        const h = self.height;
        const w = self.width;
        const c = self.channels;
        const coarse_h = h / 4;
        const coarse_w = w / 4;
        const coarse_c = c * 4;
        const coarse_dim = coarse_h * coarse_w * coarse_c;
        if (input.shape.dims.len != 2) return error.ShapeMismatch;
        if (input.shape.dims[0] != batch_size) return error.ShapeMismatch;
        if (input.shape.dims[1] != h * w * c) return error.ShapeMismatch;
        var out = try Tensor.init(allocator, &.{ batch_size, coarse_dim });
        errdefer out.deinit();
        for (0..batch_size) |b| {
            for (0..coarse_h) |oh| {
                for (0..coarse_w) |ow| {
                    for (0..c) |ic| {
                        for (0..4) |block| {
                            const ih = oh * 4 + block;
                            const in_pixel_idx = b * (h * w * c) + ih * (w * c) + ow * 4 * c + ic;
                            const out_ic = ic * 4 + block;
                            const out_pixel_idx = b * coarse_dim + oh * (coarse_w * coarse_c) + ow * coarse_c + out_ic;
                            out.data[out_pixel_idx] = input.data[in_pixel_idx];
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
        return out;
    }

    pub fn squeezeIntoMid(self: *const MultiScaleImageGenerator, input: *const Tensor, batch_size: usize, allocator: Allocator) !Tensor {
        const h = self.height;
        const w = self.width;
        const c = self.channels;
        const mid_h = h / 2;
        const mid_w = w / 2;
        const mid_c = c * 2;
        const mid_dim = mid_h * mid_w * mid_c;
        if (input.shape.dims.len != 2) return error.ShapeMismatch;
        if (input.shape.dims[0] != batch_size) return error.ShapeMismatch;
        if (input.shape.dims[1] != h * w * c) return error.ShapeMismatch;
        var out = try Tensor.init(allocator, &.{ batch_size, mid_dim });
        errdefer out.deinit();
        for (0..batch_size) |b| {
            for (0..mid_h) |oh| {
                for (0..mid_w) |ow| {
                    for (0..c) |ic| {
                        for (0..2) |block| {
                            const ih = oh * 2 + block;
                            const in_pixel_idx = b * (h * w * c) + ih * (w * c) + ow * 2 * c + ic;
                            const out_ic = ic * 2 + block;
                            const out_pixel_idx = b * mid_dim + oh * (mid_w * mid_c) + ow * mid_c + out_ic;
                            out.data[out_pixel_idx] = input.data[in_pixel_idx];
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
        return out;
    }

    pub fn generateCoarse(self: *MultiScaleImageGenerator, num_images: usize, temperature: f32, allocator: Allocator) !Tensor {
        return self.coarse.generate(num_images, temperature, allocator);
    }

    pub fn generateMid(self: *MultiScaleImageGenerator, num_images: usize, temperature: f32, allocator: Allocator) !Tensor {
        return self.mid.generate(num_images, temperature, allocator);
    }

    pub fn generateFine(self: *MultiScaleImageGenerator, num_images: usize, temperature: f32, allocator: Allocator) !Tensor {
        return self.fine.generate(num_images, temperature, allocator);
    }

    pub fn trainFineStep(self: *MultiScaleImageGenerator, raw_pixels_batch: []const []const u8, allocator: Allocator) !f32 {
        return self.fine.trainStep(raw_pixels_batch, allocator);
    }

    pub fn trainMidStep(self: *MultiScaleImageGenerator, raw_pixels_batch: []const []const u8, allocator: Allocator) !f32 {
        return self.mid.trainStep(raw_pixels_batch, allocator);
    }

    pub fn trainCoarseStep(self: *MultiScaleImageGenerator, raw_pixels_batch: []const []const u8, allocator: Allocator) !f32 {
        return self.coarse.trainStep(raw_pixels_batch, allocator);
    }
};

